{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>If</b>: Ezekiel already mentioned the matter of the watchman, for the prophet resembles him. The meaning is: how do you not tremble at the words of the prophet, or do you think that a disaster befalls a city—if I did not decree it to be? And this is: \"and YHWH did not do [it],\" for HaShem too does not bring disaster until He reveals His secret to make it known to you through the prophet—perhaps you will return from your evil ways, in the manner of \"[If] I speak for a moment concerning a nation and kingdom\" [Jeremiah 18:7]. For [at] the roar of the lion every hearer trembles—how much more so when I give forth My voice and speak to the prophet, [and] how should he not fear Me, to fulfill what I have commanded him."], :book :amos, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Amos -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/amos"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:17:55.939955291Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}